"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Breakfast & Brunch, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Coffee & Tea, Food","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"Y2Pfil51rNvTd_lFHwzb_g","review_id":"sos-JeR3bhAvfHiEmynl3g","date":"2013-02-09T13:44:26","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9557198286056519,"text_excerpt":"This is another good option for Beignets in the French Quarter. I would say to come here to avoid the massive crowds at nearby Du Monde Cafe, but the line was pretty beastly here as well. There are not nearly as many people here, since it's much smaller, but it seems like the wait is pretty bad because they serve a lot more than just beignets here. They have a pretty extensive menu consisting of several breakfast items and pastries. We just came for beignets though, to complete the trifecta of major beignets stops in New Orleans (along with Du Monde and Morning Call). These beignets were excellent, and definitely on par with the other two big names. They don't go as crazy as Du Monde does..."},{"business_id":"Y2Pfil51rNvTd_lFHwzb_g","review_id":"xInOUQTlu1EQVoI4HsFS9w","date":"2014-06-18T19:02:30","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9525331258773804,"text_excerpt":"I like this place a lot! It's cozy and welcoming. But of course I was here to try the beignets, and they do not disappoint! They came out hot and looking good. Theirs are more flat, with a slightly crunchy exterior with a gooey interior. They were really yummy, and in fact, I like theirs the best out of all the ones I tried so far. Theirs is even better than the ones at Cafe Du Monde. And I found out they use similar batter as the other place but they treat the dough different, and cook them at a lower temp, which makes a huge difference! And coffee is good too. I highly recommend this place. By the way, whenever you see local police eating at a place, it must be good!"},{"business_id":"Y2Pfil51rNvTd_lFHwzb_g","review_id":"g-j9LsKTDj6ulg6MOj0e7g","date":"2015-02-26T06:54:22","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9508798122406006,"text_excerpt":"I was referred to this place by a friendly (but slightly scary) man on the bus when I was telling him I was looking for a breakfast and beignet place near Magazine. I was surprisingly impressed by his recommendation. You can find kindness in such unexpected places! It's a tight squeeze, the line goes right down the middle of the cafe with tiny tables around the perimeter. But there is also lovely seating outside! It was just freezing at the time so I didn't get to enjoy it personally. When I went between 9:30-10am, it was busy. Maybe a 15-20 minute wait in line to order. However when we went back the following day, probably around 9am there was no line at all! Service was very friendly, t..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"Y2Pfil51rNvTd_lFHwzb_g","photo_id":"H2VzYJuzVIsIRWlIJfDeVg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/H2VzYJuzVIsIRWlIJfDeVg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8706073760986328},{"business_id":"Y2